in folding within the cell is influenced by controlled rates of polypeptide elongation</article-title><source>J Mol Biol</source><year>1992</year><volume>228</volume><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>12</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1447795</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0022-2836(92)90486-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Komar</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lesnik</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Reiss</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Synonymous codon substitutions affect ribosome traffic and protein folding during in vitro translation</article-title><source>FEBS Lett</source><year>1999</year><volume>462</volume><fpage>387</fpage><lpage>391</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10622731</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0014-5793(99)01566-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thanaraj</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Argos</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Protein secondary structural types are differentially coded on messenger RNA</article-title><source>Protein Sci</source><year>1996</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>1973</fpage><lpage>1983</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8897597</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Makhoul</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Trifonov</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution of rare triplets along mRNA and their relation to protein folding</article-title><source>J Biomol Struct Dyn</source><year>2002</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>413</fpage><lpage>420</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12437379</pub-id></citation></r